    "updated_at": "2024-09-18T21:47:20Z",
    "body": "For anyone using Fish that lands here from a Google search, you can now use:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[character]\r\nsuccess_symbol = \"[❯](bold green)\"\r\nerror_symbol = \"[❯](bold red)\"\r\nvicmd_symbol = \"[❮](bold green)\"\r\nvimcmd_replace_one_symbol = \"[❮](bold purple)\"\r\nvimcmd_replace_symbol = \"[❮](bold purple)\"\r\nvimcmd_visual_symbol = \"[❮](bold yellow)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nBUT - that ties your prompt character to your vi mode symbol. What if you want a prompt that has those two things in separate places? The answer is a custom Starship handler paired with a Fish function bound to changes to the `fish_bind_mode` variable:\r\n\r\n```fish\r\n# Put this in your config.fish\r\nfunction on_fish_bind_mode --on-variable fish_bind_mode\r\n    # export the vi_mode_symbol variable which Starship can use\r\n    set --global --export vi_mode_symbol \"\"\r\n\r\n    # Do whatever you want here to set vi_mode_symbol...\r\n    set --local color\r\n    set --local char\r\n    if test \"$fish_key_bindings\" = fish_vi_key_bindings\r\n        switch $fish_bind_mode\r\n            case default\r\n                set color red\r\n                set symbol N\r\n            case insert\r\n                set color green\r\n                set symbol I\r\n            case replace replace_one\r\n                set color green\r\n                set symbol R\r\n            case visual\r\n                set color brmagenta\r\n                set symbol V\r\n            case '*'\r\n                set color cyan\r\n                set symbol \"?\"\r\n        end\r\n        set vi_mode_symbol (set_color --bold $color)\"[$symbol]\"(set_color normal)\r\n    end\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow, add a custom section to your starship toml:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\nformat = \"\"\"${custom.vi_mode}...etc...${character}\"\"\"\r\n\r\n# Make a custom vi_mode Starship section\r\n[custom.vi_mode]\r\nformat=\"[$output]($style) \"\r\ncommand = 'echo $vi_mode_symbol'\r\nwhen = 'test -n \"$vi_mode_symbol\"'\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
